-# Canonical Kronk auth-form shell. Used by every Devise view that
-# takes a form on a Rails-served page: sign-in, forgot password,
-# reset password, resend confirmation, email setup.
-#
-# The shell handles the surrounding layout — title, lede, error
-# messages, footer links — and takes the form fields as a block.
-# Inside the block, use plain simple_form_for with `.kronk-form__*`
-# classes on inputs (see the individual view files for the
-# canonical pattern).
-#
-# Locals:
-#   title:    (required) H1 text for the page.
-#   lede:     (optional) sub-headline under the title. HAML string,
-#             may include links.
-#   footer_links: (optional, default true) render `_links.html.haml`
-#             below the form. Sign-in / password reset always want
-#             them; captcha pages sometimes don't.
-#
-# Block:
-#   The form body. Typically a `simple_form_for(...)` with
-#   `.kronk-form__field` rows inside.

:ruby
  title        = local_assigns.fetch(:title)
  lede         = local_assigns[:lede]
  footer_links = local_assigns.fetch(:footer_links, true)

.kronk-auth-shell
  %header.kronk-auth-shell__header
    %h1.kronk-auth-shell__title= title
    - if lede
      %p.kronk-auth-shell__lede= lede

  .kronk-auth-shell__body
    = yield

  - if footer_links
    .kronk-auth-shell__footer
      = render 'auth/shared/links'
